# Agent factory (Cursor rule)

This rule mirrors the `agent-factory` skill. The authoritative content lives in
[`../../SKILL.md`](../../SKILL.md) at the repo root — read it for the full schema,
compile workflow, design principles, and Mode 2 (blueprint → real skill) mapping.

**Core behavior:** when a request reads like "help me produce X" (a prompt, an
agent, a reusable spec), do **not** produce X directly. Compile the reusable
pseudocode prompt that produces X, every time, consistently:

```
<role>            expert identity + priority ordering
<goal>            concrete deliverables as outcomes, not activities
<context>         ground-truth situational facts
<inputs>          named artifacts/files/data, not "the codebase"
<task>            numbered, decomposed steps — never one sentence
<instructions>    cross-cutting behavioral rules, evidence/severity rubrics
<constraints>     what NOT to do (when scope creep is likely)
<evaluation>      how to self-judge the draft (when quality bar isn't obvious)
<output_format>   exact return shape: sections/tables/schemas > prose
<termination_condition>  explicit stop condition; label "Unknown" over guessing
```

Worked example: [`../../examples/repository-auditor.txt`](../../examples/repository-auditor.txt).

If the ask is "make this a repeatable thing I invoke", compile the blueprint
first, then convert it into a Cursor rule (`.cursor/rules/<name>.mdc`,
`alwaysApply: false` + rich `description`) or a Claude Code `SKILL.md` — see
Mode 2 in `SKILL.md`.
